===Etymology===
Probably alteration of {{m|en|change of pace}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtʃeɪndʒʌp/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[change]]-[[up]]}}

# {{label|en|baseball}} A [[pitch]] thrown with the arm motion of a [[fastball]], but which travels at a much slower velocity because it is released without the fingers adding power to the delivery.
#: ''The pitcher had a devastating '''change-up'''.''
# {{label|en|by extension}} An unexpected event.
#: ''This RFQ is a real '''change-up'''.''

